          "filename": "Guishan overlooking Banping Mountain ( WEI, WAN-CHEN ).jpg",
          "caption": "Guishan Mountain, also known as Guifengling, is located in the Zuoying District of Kaohsiung City, Taiwan. It is located in the southwestern part of Lianchi Lake. The northeast is opposite to Banping Mountain, and the southwest is adjacent to the end of Shoushan,it is a hill that runs northeast - southwest. Only 63 meters above sea level, It is a raised coral reef limestone terrain with the adjacent Banping Mountain and Shoushan. 2011 was incorporated into the Shoushan National Nature Park. The name comes from because there is a small peak at the northeast end, shaped like a turtle.",
          "alt": "Guishan Mountain, also known as Guifengling, is located in the Zuoying District of Kaohsiung City, Taiwan. It is located in the southwestern part of Lianchi Lake. The northeast is opposite to Banping Mountain, and the southwest is adjacent to the end of Shoushan,it is a hill that runs northeast - southwest. Only 63 meters above sea level, It is a raised coral reef limestone terrain with the adjacent Banping Mountain and Shoushan. 2011 was incorporated into the Shoushan National Nature Park. The name comes from because there is a small peak at the northeast end, shaped like a turtle.",
